<ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">CDD109 – Redes Neurais Artificiais e Deep Learning</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:jc ns0:val="center" /><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Professora: Profa. Dra. Sarah Negreiros de Carvalho Leite</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:jc ns0:val="center" /><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Atividade: Projeto 1 – Analisando Vinhos</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:jc ns0:val="center" /><ns0:spacing ns0:after="120" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Aluno: Leonardo Isaac Silva Flores</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">1. Base de dados Wine (Scikit-Learn)</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Carregamento da base de dados de vinhos usando datasets.load_wine() do Scikit-Learn. Os dados contêm análises químicas de vinhos de três produtores diferentes da mesma região da Itália.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="80" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:i /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Minha observação:</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">A base veio completa, sem nenhum dado faltante (NaN). São 13 características químicas medidas em laboratório (como álcool, acidez e polifenóis) e 3 tipos de vinho para identificar.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">2. Dimensão dos dados e rótulos</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">• Matriz de dados (X): dimensão (178, 13) -&gt; 178 amostras e 13 variáveis por amostra.
• Vetor de rótulos (Y): dimensão (178,) -&gt; classes 0, 1 e 2.
• Características: alcohol, malic_acid, ash, alcalinity_of_ash, magnesium, total_phenols, flavanoids, nonflavanoid_phenols, proanthocyanins, color_intensity, hue, od280/od315_of_diluted_wines, proline.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="80" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:i /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Minha observação:</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Cada linha da matriz X representa uma garrafa de vinho com suas 13 medidas químicas, e o vetor Y indica a qual dos três cultivos pertence. Temos um problema típico de classificação multiclasse com 178 exemplos.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">3. Contagem de amostras por classe</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Contagem feita com indexação lógica no NumPy (sum(Y == classe)):
• Classe 0: 59 amostras (33,1%)
• Classe 1: 71 amostras (39,9%)
• Classe 2: 48 amostras (27,0%)
• Total: 178 amostras</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="80" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:i /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Minha observação:</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">As três classes estão bem equilibradas, variando entre 48 e 71 amostras. Nenhuma classe domina a base nem fica em minoria extrema, o que facilita o treinamento de modelos e torna a acurácia uma métrica justa para avaliação.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">4. Estatísticas separadas por classe de vinho</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Os dados foram divididos em fatias conforme os limites de cada classe (x_vinho1 = X[0:59], x_vinho2 = X[59:130], x_vinho3 = X[130:178]). Em seguida, foram calculados máximo, mínimo, média e desvio padrão de cada variável (axis=0):

Principais médias encontradas:
• Álcool: Classe 0 = 13,74% | Classe 1 = 12,28% | Classe 2 = 13,15%
• Flavanoids: Classe 0 = 2,98 | Classe 1 = 2,08 | Classe 2 = 0,78
• Color Intensity: Classe 0 = 5,53 | Classe 1 = 3,09 | Classe 2 = 7,40
• Proline: Classe 0 = 1115,71 mg/L | Classe 1 = 519,51 mg/L | Classe 2 = 629,90 mg/L</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="80" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:i /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Minha observação:</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Dá para notar diferenças claras entre as classes: a classe 0 tem muito mais Proline (média 1115 contra ~500-600 das outras) e maior teor alcoólico. A classe 2 tem a cor mais intensa (7,40) e o menor nível de flavonoides (0,78). Essas diferenças mostram que as variáveis têm bom poder para separar os vinhos.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">5. Gráfico de dispersão: Flavanoids vs. Proline</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Gráfico cruzando Flavanoids (coluna 6, eixo x) com Proline (coluna 12, eixo y) para cada classe (verde = classe 0, vermelho = classe 1, azul = classe 2):</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:jc ns0:val="center" /><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:before="60" /></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:drawing><ns3:inline distT="0" distB="0" distL="0" distR="0"><ns3:extent cx="4800000" cy="3200000" /><ns3:effectExtent l="0" t="0" r="0" b="0" /><ns3:docPr id="100" name="Picture_rId8" /><ns3:cNvGraphicFramePr><ns5:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1" /></ns3:cNvGraphicFramePr><ns5:graphic><ns5:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><ns6:pic><ns6:nvPicPr><ns6:cNvPr id="100" name="" /><ns6:cNvPicPr /></ns6:nvPicPr><ns6:blipFill><ns5:blip ns7:embed="rId8" /><ns5:stretch><ns5:fillRect /></ns5:stretch></ns6:blipFill><ns6:spPr><ns5:xfrm><ns5:off x="0" y="0" /><ns5:ext cx="4800000" cy="3200000" /></ns5:xfrm><ns5:prstGeom prst="rect"><ns5:avLst /></ns5:prstGeom></ns6:spPr></ns6:pic></ns5:graphicData></ns5:graphic></ns3:inline></ns0:drawing></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="80" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:i /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Minha observação:</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Mesmo usando apenas 2 das 13 características, os três grupos já ficam praticamente separados no gráfico:
• Classe 0 (verde): fica no topo, com Proline alta e Flavanoids altos;
• Classe 1 (vermelho): fica embaixo à direita, com Proline baixa e Flavanoids médios/altos;
• Classe 2 (azul): fica embaixo à esquerda, com Flavanoids baixos e Proline intermediária.
Quase não há sobreposição entre os pontos, o que mostra que essas duas variáveis sozinhas já resolvem boa parte da classificação.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">6. Médias das classes e Distâncias Euclidianas</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Pontos médios calculados para cada classe (Flavanoids, Proline):
• Média Classe 0: [2,98; 1115,71]
• Média Classe 1: [2,08; 519,51]
• Média Classe 2: [0,78; 629,90]</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:jc ns0:val="center" /><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:before="60" /></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:drawing><ns3:inline distT="0" distB="0" distL="0" distR="0"><ns3:extent cx="4800000" cy="3200000" /><ns3:effectExtent l="0" t="0" r="0" b="0" /><ns3:docPr id="100" name="Picture_rId9" /><ns3:cNvGraphicFramePr><ns5:graphicFrameLocks noChangeAspect="1" /></ns3:cNvGraphicFramePr><ns5:graphic><ns5:graphicData uri="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/picture"><ns6:pic><ns6:nvPicPr><ns6:cNvPr id="100" name="" /><ns6:cNvPicPr /></ns6:nvPicPr><ns6:blipFill><ns5:blip ns7:embed="rId9" /><ns5:stretch><ns5:fillRect /></ns5:stretch></ns6:blipFill><ns6:spPr><ns5:xfrm><ns5:off x="0" y="0" /><ns5:ext cx="4800000" cy="3200000" /></ns5:xfrm><ns5:prstGeom prst="rect"><ns5:avLst /></ns5:prstGeom></ns6:spPr></ns6:pic></ns5:graphicData></ns5:graphic></ns3:inline></ns0:drawing></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Distâncias Euclidianas calculadas entre os pontos médios (sqrt(sum((p1 - p2)^2))):
• Distância Classe 0 - Classe 1: 596,21
• Distância Classe 0 - Classe 2: 485,82
• Distância Classe 1 - Classe 2: 110,40</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="40" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="80" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:i /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Minha observação:</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">Duas coisas chamam atenção nesses resultados:
1. As classes 1 e 2 estão muito mais próximas entre si (distância de 110,40) do que da classe 0 (quase 500 e 600).
2. A Proline varia na casa dos milhares (500 a 1100), enquanto Flavanoids varia entre 0 e 3. Por isso, a Proline domina quase 100% da conta da distância euclidiana bruta. Isso prova na prática por que precisamos normalizar os dados (StandardScaler ou MinMax) antes de rodar algoritmos como Redes Neurais: sem isso, variáveis com números grandes engolem as variáveis menores, mesmo que as menores sejam muito informativas.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" ns0:before="140" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:b /><ns0:sz ns0:val="24" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="24" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">7. Conclusão</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:p><ns0:pPr><ns0:spacing ns0:after="80" ns0:line="240" ns0:lineRule="auto" /><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /></ns0:rPr></ns0:pPr><ns0:r><ns0:rPr><ns0:rFonts ns0:ascii="Times New Roman" ns0:hAnsi="Times New Roman" ns0:cs="Times New Roman" /><ns0:sz ns0:val="22" /><ns0:szCs ns0:val="22" /></ns0:rPr><ns0:t xml:space="preserve">O exercício permitiu praticar fatiamento de matrizes, operações com NumPy e visualização com Matplotlib. A base Wine se mostrou bem comportada e facilmente separável. O cálculo das distâncias deixou evidente a necessidade de normalizar atributos com grandezas muito diferentes antes de alimentar modelos de aprendizado de máquina.</ns0:t></ns0:r></ns0:p><ns0:sectPr ns0:rsidR="003E33D5" ns0:rsidRPr="0025336F" ns0:rsidSect="002C7894"><ns0:pgSz ns0:w="11906" ns0:h="16838" /><ns0:pgMar ns0:top="709" ns0:right="1701" ns0:bottom="1417" ns0:left="1701" ns0:header="708" ns0:footer="708" ns0:gutter="0" /><ns0:cols ns0:space="708" /><ns0:docGrid ns0:linePitch="360" /></ns0:sectPr></ns0:body></ns0:document>